**When to use static members:**

| Use Case | Example |
|----------|---------|
| Counters/ID generators | `static int nextId` |
| Utility/helper functions | `MathUtils.calculate()` |
| Constants | `static final double PI` |
| Singleton pattern | `static getInstance()` |
| Factory methods | `static createFromJSON()` |
| Registry/cache | `static Map<String, User> cache` |

**Important Notes:**
- Static methods cannot access instance members directly
- Static members are loaded once in memory
- Static blocks run when class is first loaded
- Static methods cannot be overridden (but can be hidden)
- Use static for functionality not tied to specific instance
